{
  "loaded": [
    {
      "tool_id": "hirearchy::whoami",
      "description": "Your address, role, budget, direct reports, open tasks, outstanding delegations and charter.",
      "input_schema": {
        "type": "object",
        "properties": {}
      }
    },
    {
      "tool_id": "hirearchy::inbox",
      "description": "The messages for this run. For root (the human) this lists unread messages and marks them read.",
      "input_schema": {
        "type": "object",
        "properties": {}
      }
    },
    {
      "tool_id": "hirearchy::delegate",
      "description": "Assign a task to one of your direct reports.\n\n        to: the report's address (e.g. \"ceo/cto\"). title: a few words. goal: what outcome is needed and why.\n        acceptance: concrete, checkable criteria for \"done\". inputs: paths (relative to the org root) the\n        report should read. budget: runs handed to the report from your own budget. If you omit it, the default is\n        min(default_budget from ORG.md, your budget - reserve), where the reserve keeps one run per outstanding\n        delegation plus one for this one; if that is below 1 the call fails and tells you your options.\n        An explicit budget must leave that same reserve.\n        Copy the relevant acceptance criteria verbatim from the task you are working on; never paraphrase or relax them.\n        revises: when sending work back for rework, the id of the earlier task you sent to the same report.\n        Returns the task id. Do not wait for the result: end your run, the result will wake you.\n        ",
      "input_schema": {
        "type": "object",
        "properties": {
          "to": {
            "title": "To",
            "type": "string"
          },
          "title": {
            "title": "Title",
            "type": "string"
          },
          "goal": {
            "title": "Goal",
            "type": "string"
          },
          "acceptance": {
            "title": "Acceptance",
            "type": "string"
          },
          "inputs": {
            "anyOf": [
              {
                "items": {
                  "type": "string"
                },
                "type": "array"
              },
              {
                "type": "null"
              }
            ],
            "default": null,
            "title": "Inputs"
          },
          "budget": {
            "anyOf": [
              {
                "type": "integer"
              },
              {
                "type": "null"
              }
            ],
            "default": null,
            "title": "Budget"
          },
          "revises": {
            "anyOf": [
              {
                "type": "string"
              },
              {
                "type": "null"
              }
            ],
            "default": null,
            "title": "Revises"
          }
        },
        "required": [
          "to",
          "title",
          "goal",
          "acceptance"
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "tool_id": "hirearchy::report",
      "description": "Answer a task assigned to you. Goes to whoever assigned it.\n\n        status: \"done\" (every acceptance criterion verifiably met), \"failed\", or \"blocked\" (say what would unblock it).\n        `done` and `failed` are final: a second report is refused. `blocked` is not: once the blocker is resolved\n        you may report the task again, once per blocked report (any status; the new report supersedes the old one),\n        under the same rules. A `send` note never changes a task's outcome and must not claim criteria are met.\n        summary: at most ~10 lines; this is all your manager reads by default. artifacts: paths of the\n        files that hold the work; they must exist. Files in the organization: path relative to the org root.\n        Files in your workspace: the ABSOLUTE path (anything else outside the organization is refused). The runtime\n        annotates each with its word count and whether it changed since the task was assigned.\n        lessons: required when the task is a request for a service, whatever the status - done, failed or blocked\n        (1-3 lines, at most 800 characters: what worked or went wrong, what to change in the playbook, the evidence:\n        runs, rework, review findings); it is recorded in the result and reviewed before the next request. Optional\n        otherwise.\n        ",
      "input_schema": {
        "type": "object",
        "properties": {
          "task_id": {
            "title": "Task Id",
            "type": "string"
          },
          "status": {
            "title": "Status",
            "type": "string"
          },
          "summary": {
            "title": "Summary",
            "type": "string"
          },
          "artifacts": {
            "anyOf": [
              {
                "items": {
                  "type": "string"
                },
                "type": "array"
              },
              {
                "type": "null"
              }
            ],
            "default": null,
            "title": "Artifacts"
          },
          "lessons": {
            "anyOf": [
              {
                "type": "string"
              },
              {
                "type": "null"
              }
            ],
            "default": null,
            "title": "Lessons"
          }
        },
        "required": [
          "task_id",
          "status",
          "summary"
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "tool_id": "hirearchy::send",
      "description": "Send a note: a question, information, or an escalation.\n\n        Allowed recipients: your parent, your direct reports, your siblings, or the sender of the message\n        you reply to (set reply_to to its id). budget: runs to move along with the note (optional): extra runs\n        granted to a direct report, or unneeded runs given back to your PARENT (never to a sibling). Runs you\n        have left return to your parent by themselves with your final `done`/`failed` report when nothing else\n        is open for you; use this only to give some back earlier. To pull unspent runs BACK from an idle direct\n        report instead (budget stranded in a team that cannot use it), use `reclaim`.\n        ",
      "input_schema": {
        "type": "object",
        "properties": {
          "to": {
            "title": "To",
            "type": "string"
          },
          "body": {
            "title": "Body",
            "type": "string"
          },
          "title": {
            "default": "",
            "title": "Title",
            "type": "string"
          },
          "reply_to": {
            "anyOf": [
              {
                "type": "string"
              },
              {
                "type": "null"
              }
            ],
            "default": null,
            "title": "Reply To"
          },
          "budget": {
            "default": 0,
            "title": "Budget",
            "type": "integer"
          }
        },
        "required": [
          "to",
          "body"
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "tool_id": "hirearchy::reclaim",
      "description": "Pull unspent budget back from one of your DIRECT reports (a manager from its team; root from its top agents).\n\n        report: its short name or address. budget: how many runs (default: all it has left). Only an idle report:\n        no open task, nothing delegated and outstanding, not running, no unread mail that would wake it; otherwise the\n        call is refused and says why. Not from deeper down (a manager reclaims from its own reports). The report is\n        not woken and gets no message; you get the runs (they join your budget at once, and then a delegation or\n        `send(..., budget=N)` can move them to whoever needs them). Use it before asking your parent for more runs\n        while a sibling team sits on unspent ones.\n        ",
      "input_schema": {
        "type": "object",
        "properties": {
          "report": {
            "title": "Report",
            "type": "string"
          },
          "budget": {
            "anyOf": [
              {
                "type": "integer"
              },
              {
                "type": "null"
              }
            ],
            "default": null,
            "title": "Budget"
          }
        },
        "required": [
          "report"
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "tool_id": "hirearchy::hire",
      "description": "Create a direct report (only if your charter allows hiring).\n\n        name: lowercase-dashed (becomes the address <you>/<name>). role: a short job title.\n        charter: markdown with purpose, responsibilities, decision rights, what to escalate, quality bar.\n        model: kiro model id (optional; unset = the organization's default model, claude-sonnet-5.5). tools: kiro built-in tools to grant, only ones you have yourself\n        (e.g. \"read\", \"write\", \"shell\"). can_hire: whether the report may build its own team; only root (the user) or an approved plan can grant it.\n        max_children: the most direct reports it may have (for an agent hiring: at most its own); a report without can_hire gets 0.\n        workspace: directory the report works in (must be inside yours).\n        inputs: absolute folders the report may only READ (never change); a manager can give only folders inside its\n        own inputs or workspace. A report with `read` and no workspace/inputs reads nothing outside the org.\n        A new report has no budget until you delegate a task to it.\n        ",
      "input_schema": {
        "type": "object",
        "properties": {
          "name": {
            "title": "Name",
            "type": "string"
          },
          "role": {
            "title": "Role",
            "type": "string"
          },
          "charter": {
            "title": "Charter",
            "type": "string"
          },
          "model": {
            "anyOf": [
              {
                "type": "string"
              },
              {
                "type": "null"
              }
            ],
            "default": null,
            "title": "Model"
          },
          "tools": {
            "anyOf": [
              {
                "items": {
                  "type": "string"
                },
                "type": "array"
              },
              {
                "type": "null"
              }
            ],
            "default": null,
            "title": "Tools"
          },
          "can_hire": {
            "default": false,
            "title": "Can Hire",
            "type": "boolean"
          },
          "max_children": {
            "default": 5,
            "title": "Max Children",
            "type": "integer"
          },
          "workspace": {
            "anyOf": [
              {
                "type": "string"
              },
              {
                "type": "null"
              }
            ],
            "default": null,
            "title": "Workspace"
          },
          "inputs": {
            "anyOf": [
              {
                "items": {
                  "type": "string"
                },
                "type": "array"
              },
              {
                "type": "null"
              }
            ],
            "default": null,
            "title": "Inputs"
          }
        },
        "required": [
          "name",
          "role",
          "charter"
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "tool_id": "hirearchy::retire",
      "description": "Remove a direct report and its team (name: its short name or full address, e.g. \"eng\" or \"ceo/eng\").\n\n        Their open tasks are reported to you as failed, and the team's unspent budget is returned to you.\n        ",
      "input_schema": {
        "type": "object",
        "properties": {
          "name": {
            "title": "Name",
            "type": "string"
          },
          "reason": {
            "title": "Reason",
            "type": "string"
          }
        },
        "required": [
          "name",
          "reason"
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "tool_id": "hirearchy::org_read",
      "description": "The ORGANIZATION's read tool (kiro shows it as @hirearchy/org_read; not kiro's built-in `read`, which reads the\n        workspace). kiro's built-in file tools (`read_file`, `list_directory`) read the workspace, inputs and, by absolute path, the organization; this tool is the organization's relative-path reader, called `org_read` for you. Reads a file (with word count and modification time) or lists a directory in the organization. Paths\n        are relative to the org root, e.g. \"ceo/writer/work/brief.md\". Outside the organization only ABSOLUTE paths work,\n        and only inside your workspace, your read-only inputs, or the workspace of an agent in your team (to verify\n        what your reports made); anything else is refused.",
      "input_schema": {
        "type": "object",
        "properties": {
          "path": {
            "default": ".",
            "title": "Path",
            "type": "string"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "tool_id": "hirearchy::write",
      "description": "Write an ORGANIZATION file (kiro shows this tool as @hirearchy/write; it is NOT kiro's built-in `write`, which\n        writes the workspace). Use it for your memory, notes and artifacts inside your own org directory. Paths are\n        relative to the org root, like every path here, so they start with your address: e.g. \"<you>/MEMORY.md\" or\n        \"<you>/work/plan.md\".\n\n        You may also rewrite a direct report's charter (\"<you>/<name>/AGENT.md\"). Inboxes, logs and your own\n        charter are managed by the runtime; use send/delegate/report to communicate. A charter rewrite keeps every\n        frontmatter key (tools, inputs, model, ...) that your new text does not set; the reply lists what was kept\n        and what changed.\n        ",
      "input_schema": {
        "type": "object",
        "properties": {
          "path": {
            "title": "Path",
            "type": "string"
          },
          "content": {
            "title": "Content",
            "type": "string"
          },
          "append": {
            "default": false,
            "title": "Append",
            "type": "boolean"
          }
        },
        "required": [
          "path",
          "content"
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "tool_id": "hirearchy::status",
      "description": "The whole organization as a tree: each agent's role, state, budget and workload.",
      "input_schema": {
        "type": "object",
        "properties": {}
      }
    },
    {
      "tool_id": "hirearchy::health",
      "description": "Health report (stuck, expensive, low-quality, wasteful, idle, paused) for an agent and its subtree.\n\n        agent: yourself or an agent in your own subtree (root may ask about anyone). Default: your own subtree\n        (root: the whole organization). Use it to decide whom to follow up with, rework, re-budget or retire.\n        ",
      "input_schema": {
        "type": "object",
        "properties": {
          "agent": {
            "anyOf": [
              {
                "type": "string"
              },
              {
                "type": "null"
              }
            ],
            "default": null,
            "title": "Agent"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "tool_id": "hirearchy::services",
      "description": "The standing services you can request from your direct reports and the ones you offer, with contract and\n        playbook versions, inputs, budget per request and the record so far (requests, outcomes, runs, feedback).",
      "input_schema": {
        "type": "object",
        "properties": {}
      }
    },
    {
      "tool_id": "hirearchy::define_service",
      "description": "Define a standing service of one of your direct reports (root: a top-level agent), or amend its contract.\n\n        You are the client: the contract is yours; the owner cannot change it. owner: the report. name: lowercase-dashed,\n        unique among your reports' services. FIRST definition needs description (one line), acceptance (concrete,\n        checkable criteria that travel with every request), deliverable ({description, format?, max_words?, path?\n        (absolute)}) and budget (runs handed down with each request); optional: inputs ([{name, description, required\n        (default true)}] the requester fills in), playbook (markdown workflow, first definition only), locked (true = the\n        owner may not revise the playbook), notes (free text for the owner).\n        AMENDMENT (the service exists): pass only what changes, the rest stays. To add a lasting requirement:\n        `add_acceptance=[<criterion>]`; to drop one: `remove_acceptance=[<its exact text>]`; `acceptance` replaces\n        all (not together with add/remove). The old contract is archived and the owner quietly told what changed; the\n        reply lists the criteria now in force. An amendment that changes nothing is refused.\n        ",
      "input_schema": {
        "type": "object",
        "properties": {
          "owner": {
            "title": "Owner",
            "type": "string"
          },
          "name": {
            "title": "Name",
            "type": "string"
          },
          "description": {
            "anyOf": [
              {
                "type": "string"
              },
              {
                "type": "null"
              }
            ],
            "default": null,
            "title": "Description"
          },
          "acceptance": {
            "anyOf": [
              {
                "items": {
                  "type": "string"
                },
                "type": "array"
              },
              {
                "type": "null"
              }
            ],
            "default": null,
            "title": "Acceptance"
          },
          "deliverable": {
            "anyOf": [
              {
                "additionalProperties": true,
                "type": "object"
              },
              {
                "type": "null"
              }
            ],
            "default": null,
            "title": "Deliverable"
          },
          "budget": {
            "anyOf": [
              {
                "type": "integer"
              },
              {
                "type": "null"
              }
            ],
            "default": null,
            "title": "Budget"
          },
          "inputs": {
            "anyOf": [
              {
                "items": {
                  "additionalProperties": true,
                  "type": "object"
                },
                "type": "array"
              },
              {
                "type": "null"
              }
            ],
            "default": null,
            "title": "Inputs"
          },
          "playbook": {
            "anyOf": [
              {
                "type": "string"
              },
              {
                "type": "null"
              }
            ],
            "default": null,
            "title": "Playbook"
          },
          "locked": {
            "anyOf": [
              {
                "type": "boolean"
              },
              {
                "type": "null"
              }
            ],
            "default": null,
            "title": "Locked"
          },
          "notes": {
            "anyOf": [
              {
                "type": "string"
              },
              {
                "type": "null"
              }
            ],
            "default": null,
            "title": "Notes"
          },
          "add_acceptance": {
            "anyOf": [
              {
                "items": {
                  "type": "string"
                },
                "type": "array"
              },
              {
                "type": "null"
              }
            ],
            "default": null,
            "title": "Add Acceptance"
          },
          "remove_acceptance": {
            "anyOf": [
              {
                "items": {
                  "type": "string"
                },
                "type": "array"
              },
              {
                "type": "null"
              }
            ],
            "default": null,
            "title": "Remove Acceptance"
          }
        },
        "required": [
          "owner",
          "name"
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "tool_id": "hirearchy::request",
      "description": "Ask a direct report for one of its services (see `services`): a task built from the contract.\n\n        inputs: {input name: value}; required ones must be present. note: free text for the owner. extra_acceptance:\n        criteria added after the contract's (the contract's always apply). budget: runs handed down (default: the\n        contract's; the usual reserve rule applies). revises: id of an earlier request of this service to send back for\n        rework; the reply then states the case total (runs used by the whole chain, runs handed down, the contract's\n        budget per request) and tells you to inform the user when the case exceeds that budget. Returns the task id;\n        the result comes back like any result, then rate it with `feedback`.\n        ",
      "input_schema": {
        "type": "object",
        "properties": {
          "service": {
            "title": "Service",
            "type": "string"
          },
          "inputs": {
            "anyOf": [
              {
                "additionalProperties": true,
                "type": "object"
              },
              {
                "type": "null"
              }
            ],
            "default": null,
            "title": "Inputs"
          },
          "title": {
            "default": "",
            "title": "Title",
            "type": "string"
          },
          "note": {
            "default": "",
            "title": "Note",
            "type": "string"
          },
          "extra_acceptance": {
            "anyOf": [
              {
                "items": {
                  "type": "string"
                },
                "type": "array"
              },
              {
                "type": "null"
              }
            ],
            "default": null,
            "title": "Extra Acceptance"
          },
          "budget": {
            "anyOf": [
              {
                "type": "integer"
              },
              {
                "type": "null"
              }
            ],
            "default": null,
            "title": "Budget"
          },
          "revises": {
            "anyOf": [
              {
                "type": "string"
              },
              {
                "type": "null"
              }
            ],
            "default": null,
            "title": "Revises"
          }
        },
        "required": [
          "service"
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "tool_id": "hirearchy::feedback",
      "description": "Tell the owner of a service whether a delivered request was good: verdict \"accept\" or \"reject\".\n\n        task_id: a service request (or rework) you sent that has a result. note: required for reject (what was wrong),\n        optional for accept. It costs no run and does not wake the owner; it shows up in the evidence the owner reviews\n        before its next request (and the moment a rejection arrives). Give it on your own judgement of each delivery,\n        also on a rework: every verdict stays in the case's history, the latest one is the final verdict, and an\n        earlier reject is still shown to the owner with your words. Feedback is for reflection only: it never waives an\n        acceptance criterion or changes the outcome of the request.\n        ",
      "input_schema": {
        "type": "object",
        "properties": {
          "task_id": {
            "title": "Task Id",
            "type": "string"
          },
          "verdict": {
            "title": "Verdict",
            "type": "string"
          },
          "note": {
            "default": "",
            "title": "Note",
            "type": "string"
          }
        },
        "required": [
          "task_id",
          "verdict"
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "tool_id": "hirearchy::revise_playbook",
      "description": "Write the next version of the playbook of a service you offer: how your team delivers it.\n\n        Only the owner can; refused when the contract is locked. content: the WHOLE new playbook in markdown (steps: who\n        does what, in which order, which check; budget plan; pitfalls), at most playbook_max_words (default 1000) words,\n        and different from the current one. reason: 1-400 characters naming the cases it rests on. evidence (required):\n        the ids it rests on, from the regression list and the digest in your prompt: \"R<k>\" (a rejection by the client),\n        \"C<k>\" (a contract criterion), verdict ids, case ids. It is admitted only when the same criterion or regression\n        assertion failed in 2 different cases the client rejected, or when it cites a criterion your parent added to the\n        contract by an amendment the client confirmed (your Reflect section and the amendment note name them); your\n        lessons, relayed verdicts and an agent client's verdicts are not evidence. Pass evidence=[] only for the first\n        playbook (the steps your team followed, nothing more), or to restore unchanged a version your parent wrote. A\n        refusal writes nothing and gives you a question to send your parent once; do not wait for the answer (it reaches\n        you as a contract change or a criterion link). The old version is archived; your parent is told quietly. The\n        playbook may raise the bar, never lower it: the acceptance criteria come from the contract. Returns the new\n        version, which applies from now on.\n        ",
      "input_schema": {
        "type": "object",
        "properties": {
          "service": {
            "title": "Service",
            "type": "string"
          },
          "content": {
            "title": "Content",
            "type": "string"
          },
          "reason": {
            "title": "Reason",
            "type": "string"
          },
          "evidence": {
            "items": {
              "type": "string"
            },
            "title": "Evidence",
            "type": "array"
          }
        },
        "required": [
          "service",
          "content",
          "reason",
          "evidence"
        ]
      }
    }
  ],
  "not_found": [],
  "note": "These tools are now loaded for the rest of this session. To RUN one, call tool_call with { \"tool_id\": \"namespace::tool\", \"arguments\": { ... } } (use the tool_id shown for each result, and arguments matching its input_schema). Do not call tool_load again for tools you have already loaded."
}
